|display=200x200px
|description3='''Preecha kicks a tornado forward in an arc'''
* All versions stay on screen for a very long time, good for getting in or for oki, but quite bad at actually zoning since it does not go full screen.
* The windup of the D and B+D versions already form a projectile hitbox that eats others without stopping Preecha's tornado from coming out, which can potentially cover your approach for up to two fireballs from the opponent. D version is combo-friendly and allows consistent links into Preecha's P = mc2 super
* D and B+D versions can be braked after the first tornado appears. This is useful point-blank to squeeze in a throw when the opponent is expecting the second tornado, or to make the first hit plus with spacing or a meaty timing.
* Avoid using D and B+D versions in neutral as the start-up and recovery are extremely long. Use the B version for screen control and zoning. The D and B+D versions could be used in fireball wars, but use them only to absorb an opponent's fireball as doing them raw is very risky.
* When executing this move after a forward dash, input a Tiger Knee motion (2369) to avoid accidentally doing a DP.
*The D version is Preecha's best blockstring ender. Due to being safe and frame trapping off lights,and even setting up a small RPS situation on block with breaking the second hit. The BD version is great to set up Circular step mixups on block.
