==Super Special Moves==
====Screw Archimedes Spiral====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|moveId=preecha_236236a,preecha_236236a_2,preecha_236236c,preecha_236236c_2
|captions=<br>Attack animation,<br>C super flash
|input=236236A/C
|input2=qcfqcf+A/C
|display=160x200px
|description4=Throw out a few bruising uppercuts, then finish off with a tornado.
----
A version : Preecha's 1 bar metered reversal option and combo ender
* Good as an anti-air but painfully unreliable as a reversal, it has a random chance to forego the tornados on the first two uppercuts, which increases the damage but basically halves its range and makes it drop against extended hurtboxes.
* Airborne opponents sometimes drop out of the tornado in specific angles, so even as an anti-air it can be annoying to use.
* ''Sometimes'' Preecha's highest damage one-bar ender, when it feels like it. On top of the lower frame advantage in comparison to 236236B and just how much more consistent that super is, you're probably better off not using this one outside of reversaling through blockstrings and some anti-airing.

----
C version : The most damaging fully invincible option preecha has outside of Hidden Gear.
* Similar to 236236A, has a random chance to do higher damage for no reason. Thankfully its hitboxes remain intact, and are significantly larger, so it's much better for defense.
* The randomly stronger version also has slightly better frame advantage (+34 from +33 against grounded opponents), which is variable in the first place against airborne opponents. It's hard to tell the versions apart as well, so don't use this for setups.
* Regardless of the varied advantage, it keeps the corner and leaves you +33 at the very least, which makes it preferable to 236236D as a cashout that won't necessarily kill.

}}

====P = mc<sup>2</sup>====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|moveId=preecha_236236b,preecha_236236d
|input=236236B/D
|input2=qcfqcf+B/D
|captions=<br>Attack animation,<br>D super flash
|display=200x120px
|description2=Preecha's horizontal super.
----
B Version : A far-reaching super that sideswitches unless the opponent is backed against the corner.
* ''Is NOT projectile invulnerable.'' Still a useful punish or conversion super with its high range.
* Very easy to confirm, will connect from basically any normal cancel, and its reach can help pick up normally unrewarding hits like a distant fireball.
* While less damaging than 236236A can be, it can be used as an ender in combos where 236236A would miss, which generally net more damage on top of actually being consistent.
* +40 on most hits but +42 if combo'd after a 623D break. Both are consistent and useful for setting up a powerful meaty.
* Should use this super in 99% of Preecha's combos as it is very combo-friendly and is her highest damage 1 bar ender.
----
D Version : Nearly full-screen invincible super.
* Preecha's best reversal and a useful combo ender. 
* A rewarding punish if you react to an opponent throwing a fireball or whiffing something with long recovery.
* Can be braked by pressing A+B right after the first hit connects. The following combo will do lower damage than the full super, but you can secure oki from it or keep the corner.
* Unlike 236236B, it ALWAYS sideswitches (even in the corner) provided you don't brake it. 
}}

==Hidden Gear==
==== Preecha's Last Theorem ====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|moveId=preecha_236236rev
|description=An invincible projectile.
* Can only be executed with S.P.G active and two bars, but is your most damaging combo ender with the highest minimum damage.
* While its initial range is somewhat limited, it's still pretty easy to juggle into off of almost any special thanks to its speed.
* Does eventually go further but this is mostly irrelevant, if this is fast enough to punish something at range you probably have better options.
* Actually very active and technically possible to be made plus, which is completely useless but you can occasionally be funny with it and find meaty setups.
}}

